-- title:
--   The collective spin operators $S^{[n]}_\alpha=\tfrac12\sum_i\sigma^{(i)}_\alpha$
-- statement:
--   For $n$ qubits and $\alpha\in\{x,y,z\}$ the **collective spin operator** is
--   $$
--   S^{[n]}_\alpha=\frac12\sum_{i=1}^n\sigma^{(i)}_\alpha .
--   $$
--   Strong collective decoherence is the noise whose operator algebra is generated by $I,S^{[n]}_x,S^{[n]}_y,S^{[n]}_z$; the operators commuting with all three collective spins preserve every decoherence-free subsystem. The raising and lowering operators are $S_\pm=S_x\pm iS_y$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\alpha=x,y,z$ is $0,1,2$; qubits are indexed from $0$.
-- source:
--   Bacon, Decoherence, Control, and Symmetry in Quantum Computers, arXiv:quant-ph/0305025v1, eq. (8.30), §8.4, p.113 (PDF p.130); §9.1.2, p.125 (PDF p.142)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_BaconThesis_ExchangeUniv_pauli
import Definitions.Def_BaconThesis_Collective_onQubit

open scoped Matrix

namespace BaconThesis.ExchangeUniv

/-- **The collective spin operators `S_α^[n]`.**
Bacon, *Decoherence, Control, and Symmetry in Quantum Computers*, arXiv:quant-ph/0305025v1, (8.30), §8.4, p.113 (PDF p.130): `S_α^[n] = ½ Σ_{i=1}^n σ_α^(i)`; strong collective
decoherence has the algebra generated by `{I, S_x^[n], S_y^[n], S_z^[n]}`, §9.1.2, p.125 (PDF p.142).

`collS n α` is `½ Σ_i σ_α^(i)` on `ℂ^(Fin n → Fin 2)` for `α ∈ {x, y, z} = {0, 1, 2}`.

**Formalization Note.** Qubits are indexed from `0`. The raising operator of (D.5)–(D.6),
`S_+ = S_x + iS_y`, is written `collS n 0 + Complex.I • collS n 1` where it is used. -/
noncomputable def collS (n : ℕ) (α : Fin 3) : Matrix (Fin n → Fin 2) (Fin n → Fin 2) ℂ :=
  (1 / 2 : ℂ) • ∑ i : Fin n, BaconThesis.Collective.onQubit i (pauli α)

end BaconThesis.ExchangeUniv


